{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RHLW-2026-7cb565d499929657","published":"2026-10-13T20:35:24Z","modified":"2026-11-06T19:43:12.440732746Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-54284","CVE-2026-59893","CVE-2026-59894","CVE-2026-71491","CVE-2026-84305","GHSA-3496-9g83-7v6x","GHSA-cfqr-cjx5-5jcm","GHSA-f2ff-p2ww-7p4p","GHSA-prg7-hcfm-mfcr","GHSA-pwgv-4x5q-6m9f"],"summary":"Lightwell Security Advisory: sqlparse 0.5.5+rhlw.1","details":"Red Hat Lightwell has released sqlparse 0.5.5+rhlw.1 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-54284, CVE-2026-59893, CVE-2026-59894, CVE-2026-71491, and CVE-2026-84305.\n\nCVE-2026-54284: sqlparse: TokenList.__init__ materializes O(subtree) value per group, causing CPU DoS before depth/token caps trigger\n\nCVE-2026-59893: sqlparse: Inefficient Regex Handling of Dollar-Quoted SQL Literals Leads to ReDoS (Denial of Service)\n\nCVE-2026-59894: sqlparse: Generated Python and PHP snippets allow SQL string breakout through unescaped backslashes\n\nCVE-2026-71491: sqlparse: Quadratic O(n²) DoS in group_comments\n\nCVE-2026-84305: sqlparse: Reindentation of tuple lists causes near-cap quadratic CPU consumption\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for sqlparse 0.5.5 from PyPI.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"sqlparse","ecosystem":"Red Hat Lightwell:PyPI","purl":"pkg:pypi/sqlparse"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.5.5+rhlw.1"}]}],"versions":["0.1.0","0.1.1","0.1.10","0.1.11","0.1.12","0.1.13","0.1.14","0.1.15","0.1.16","0.1.17","0.1.18","0.1.19","0.1.2","0.1.3","0.1.4","0.1.5","0.1.6","0.1.7","0.1.8","0.1.9","0.2.0","0.2.1","0.2.2","0.2.3","0.2.4","0.3.0","0.3.1","0.4.0","0.4.1","0.4.2","0.4.3","0.4.4","0.5.0","0.5.1","0.5.2","0.5.3","0.5.4","0.5.5"],"database_specific":{"lightwell":{"backport_base_version":"0.5.5","remediated_version":"0.5.5+rhlw.1","repository_url":"https://packages.redhat.com/lightwell/python/remediated/"},"source":"https://github.com/project-lightwell/lightwell-osv/blob/main/advisories/RHLW-2026